    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24328" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter-mĕo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to go between</i>, <i>flow</i> or <i>pass through the midst of;</i>
			with acc. (Plin. and late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pergamum intermeat Selinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 30, 33, § 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paludem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 11, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saepe,</span>”
				<i>to visit often</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 26, 6, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
